PROPOSAL: product-direction decision for the maintainer; do not implement without a go-ahead.

Evidence: arguments replace CMD (`--wiki-root /wiki`), and mcp-wiki defaults to '.', which is WORKDIR /home/appuser (Dockerfile:41, :58; bin/mcp-wiki:11). MCP_WIKI_ROOT is read only by the entrypoint. `docker run -i -v ...:/wiki raudssus/mcp-wiki --git` serves /home/appuser; with --rm all writes are lost. The entrypoint stats and chowns /wiki even when --wiki-root points elsewhere. (README now tells users to repeat --wiki-root.)
Options: (a) WORKDIR /wiki so the default '.' is the volume, and the entrypoint takes the owner from the effective --wiki-root; (b) mcp-wiki defaults to $ENV{MCP_WIKI_ROOT} when set (new CLI behaviour); (c) document only (done in README).
Recommendation: (a).

2026-10-26 19:51 Decision (coordinator, on the maintainer's order to work the board off): option (a): WORKDIR /wiki; the entrypoint checks the effective --wiki-root. Branch docker.
